Subject: menu: a finger's drag scrolls by its size, and a tap off the item is LEFT/RIGHT or nothing

D-083. The user, on the phone: "there's no way to scroll down, and taps on the left
or right will register as a tap on the item menu when it should just go RIGHT or
LEFT to next menu." The engine half of the fix (the other half, the click moving
from touch-down to the lift, is the shell's - app/ios/PDTouchOverlay.m):

  - inputs.mousescroll was built from the two wheel KEYS, which can only say
    "at least one", so a thumb that dragged nine rows in a frame moved the
    menu one line. While the touch pointer is live, menu.c takes the latched
    tick COUNT instead (inputIosPointerWheelTicks()), capped at 8 a frame.
    Every reader already multiplies it: LINEHEIGHT for an item-scrolled
    dialog, LINEHEIGHT+1 for a smooth-scrolled one, a row for a list, a step
    for a slider. menuIosRowFraction() tells the shell how big a tick is on
    screen, so the content follows the finger.
  - A list stepped by a drag stops at its ends instead of wrapping.
  - A click on a LIST item chooses the entry under it. A list is one menu
    item whose entries are drawn around its current index, so the focus walk
    stops at the list and the click chose the centred entry wherever it
    landed (tapping "New Agent..." under "Dark" loaded Dark). The render's
    own geometry (menuitemListRender, menuitem0f0e5d2c) maps the point back.
  - Upstream's "click beside the menu rotates it" only counts when the click
    is level with the dialog (menu.c, after the pad loop). For the touch
    pointer, left/right of the dialog is LEFT/RIGHT at ANY height, and a click
    that is not on the focused item (above/below the dialog, its header, a
    gap) is swallowed instead of being an Accept on whatever was highlighted.
    A dimmed dialog (slider/dropdown being edited) keeps upstream's rule.

Everything is inside PLATFORM_IOS.

